h better than they were post-paris  agreement as we just saw in that graphic  but it's simply still not enough what  more do you think needs to be done and  can be done  i think one of the start things that  comes through in the report is the  difference between developed and  developing countries so most of that  investment in clean energy is happening  in developed countries and china and the  developing countries investment is very  much  clean energy investment is very flat  they don't have the same resources and  if we really want to tackle this climate  crisis we will have to make sure that  those finances flow to those countries  in order to to allow them to increase  their renewable energy sources  i think the other thing finances  in terms of the types of energy sources  renewable i mean there's a lot of focus  on solar and wind but beyond that we  just mentioned hydrogen and other  sources can you tell us about what types  of energy needs to be invested in  well i think all of the above but i  think one of the things i would like to  point out is we need to be very aware  when we're making these investments and  not everything is what it what it  appears at first glance so hydrogen can  play an important role but even green  hydrogen made from renewable energy  renewable electricity so it can have a  global warming impact if we don't make  sure that we use it effectively so none  of these is a silver bullet we need to  think about what we're doing and with  renewable sources it's very important  they're very place-based you know if  you've got a lot of sun then solar is  obviously the first place to look if you  have a lot of wind or or tidal then you  know those those are other alternatives  um the other thing that is extremely  important is you know making our  buildings and our industries and our  appliances as efficient as possible we  need to get you know as much as we can  out of the electricity that we produce  so we need to make sure those renewables  are really working hard for us  jill duggan executive director from the  environmental defense fund europe thanks  very much indeed for joining us on the  daily climate show  thank you  and that's all from us for now thanks  for watching
 

